### event-service — example requests
# event/event-service-with-loco — "person-style" layout (src/api/rest/).
# Envelope: {"success":bool,"data":...,"error":...} — data/error ALWAYS
# both present (never omitted), same shape as person/worker (src/api/mod.rs).
# Gated by EVENT_REQUIRE_AUTH (default off). No review-queue HTTP surface
# and no cross-service links for this crate (capability matrix).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8085
@eventId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@token = REPLACE_WITH_BEARER_FROM_00-auth-handshake.http


### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health


### Who am I — always requires a valid bearer token (curl-verified 401
# "missing authorization header" with none, regardless of
# EVENT_REQUIRE_AUTH — see person.http for the same pattern).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Create an event — minimal valid body (id/active/name have no
# #[serde(default)]; everything else defaults).
# @name createEvent
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/events
Content-Type: application/json
Accepts-version: 1.0

{
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "active": true,
  "name": "Demo Conference",
  "start_date": "2026-06-01T18:00:00Z",
  "end_date": "2026-06-01T20:00:00Z",
  "event_status": "scheduled",
  "event_attendance_mode": "offline",
  "event_type": "conference",
  "all_day": false
}


### Get the created event back
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events/{{eventId}}


### Search events — `q` is REQUIRED (not Option) for this crate, unlike
# place/thing's optional `q`.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events/search?q=Conference&limit=10


### Update an event
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/events/{{eventId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "{{eventId}}",
  "active": true,
  "name": "Demo Conference (rescheduled)",
  "start_date": "2026-06-02T18:00:00Z",
  "end_date": "2026-06-02T20:00:00Z",
  "event_status": "scheduled",
  "event_attendance_mode": "offline",
  "event_type": "conference",
  "all_day": false
}


### Probabilistic + deterministic match
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/events/match
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "active": true,
  "name": "Demo Conference",
  "start_date": "2026-06-01T18:00:00Z",
  "end_date": "2026-06-01T20:00:00Z",
  "event_status": "scheduled",
  "event_attendance_mode": "offline",
  "event_type": "conference",
  "all_day": false
}


### Explicit duplicate check (same body shape as match)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/events/check-duplicates
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "active": true,
  "name": "Demo Conference",
  "start_date": "2026-06-01T18:00:00Z",
  "end_date": "2026-06-01T20:00:00Z",
  "event_status": "scheduled",
  "event_attendance_mode": "offline",
  "event_type": "conference",
  "all_day": false
}


### Batch deduplicate — scans the whole index
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/events/deduplicate


### Merge two confirmed-duplicate events (destructive)
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/events/merge
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "main_id": "{{eventId}}", "duplicate_id": "<other-uuid>" }


### Masked view
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events/{{eventId}}/masked


### GDPR export
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events/{{eventId}}/export


### Audit trail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events/{{eventId}}/audit


### FHIR R5 — read this event as an Appointment resource (schema.org/Event
# has no direct FHIR analogue; Appointment is the documented best-effort
# mapping, agents/share/fhir.md §3).
GET {{baseUrl}}/fhir/Appointment/{{eventId}}


### Delete (soft-delete) an event
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/events/{{eventId}}
